# 65 — Functional documentation

## Purpose
Every module the agent creates or changes has a functional doc, and that doc matches the code when
the task ends.

## When it applies
Every task in `passion-api` that creates or changes code in a module, section or workflow: a new
feature, a new section of an existing module, an endpoint, a bug fix, a permission, status, money
rule, schema the product relies on, or side effect. It also applies when the same task changes
`../passion`.

Not needed for: formatting or comment-only edits, test-only edits, and edits to `.cursor/rules/`,
`.cursor/skills/` or the docs themselves.

## Doc map
One description per feature. Do not copy it into both repos. All functional docs live in `docs/`.

| The module / change is about | Doc |
